      "writtenOn": "2019-01-08T17:20:53Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e Without marking them as register, the compiler would save these value to the stack (and read them back). Marking them as register let\u0027s the compiler skip this step (and just keep the values in a register\n\nI understand what it\u0027s doing, but it is unnecessary (as you noted below). We should allow the compiler to optimize accordingly. \n\n\u003e \n\u003e It also appears that we are compiling this (and all other EC code) with -O0 instead of -O3. If we were to move to -O1 or -O3, then I think that the compiler wouldn\u0027t write the values to the stack in that case as well.\n\nThis is broken. At the very least we should be compiling with -O2 always. And if we have register pressure we should be employing -fomit-frame-pointer as well.\n\n\u003e \n\u003e Basically adding register keyword here made the assembly smaller for this function and __hw_clock_source_read\n\nFix the optimization settings. There\u0027s no reason to decorate variables like this.",
