      "message": "Isn\u0027t that what read_main_timer() is doing? Though, it is assuming that when a !\u003d b the next read won\u0027t roll over. I\u0027m not sure that\u0027s a great assumption though. It really should be a while loop waiting until there isn\u0027t roll over.\n\nWhat is the hpet\u0027s counter size and actual tick rate? Seems like we are optimizing for precision of counter but because of the core not aligning to hpet register sizes, we\u0027re just burning cycles on every read.\n\nAny reason we aren\u0027t caching the upper 32-bits and just using 32-bit arithmetic when the cached value matches or keeping a diff such that one can quickly calculate microseconds from it?",
